                            "ge_se_pa1_clipp_stalled  :  ready to send a CLIPP transfer, but stalled by the PA (means the max number of primitives are in flight). If there are stalls on this interface we don't have a deep enough FIFO to hide VS latency from the start to position export or there is back pressure from downstream. Usually the SC in this case, but sometimes due to clipping. " = 0x38, 
                            "ge_se_pa1_clipp_starved_busy  :  CLIPP interface is starved while the VGT is busy (most accurate with VS only tests since these have the least time between the VGT going busy and the CLIPP receiving work. If looking at counts from a single draw use vgt_perf_vgt_pa_clipp_starved_after_work) " = 0x39, 
