                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_SNOOP  :  Number of snoop transactions (either 32-byte or 64-byte) going over the GL2C_EA_wrreq interface. " = 0x54, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_64B  :  Number of 64-byte transactions going (64-byte write or CMPSWAP) over the TC_EA_wrreq interface. " = 0x55, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_PROBE_COMMAND  :  Number of probe commands going over the TC_EA_wrreq interface. " = 0x56, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WR_UNCACHED_32B  :  Number of 32-byte write/atomic going over the TC_EA_wrreq interface due to uncached traffic.  Note that CC mtypes can produce uncached requests, and those are included in this. A 64-byte request will be counted as 2 " = 0x57, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MC_WRREQ_STALL  :  Number of cycles a write request was stalled. " = 0x58, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_IO_CREDIT_STALL  :  Number of cycles a EA write request was stalled because the interface was out of IO credits. " = 0x59, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_GMI_CREDIT_STALL  :  Number of cycles a EA write request was stalled because the interface was out of GMI credits. " = 0x5a, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_DRAM_CREDIT_STALL  :  Number of cycles a EA write request was stalled because the interface was out of DRAM credits. " = 0x5b, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TOO_MANY_EA_WRREQS_STALL  :  Number of cycles the GL2C could not send a EA write request because it already reached its maximum number of pending EA write requests. " = 0x5c, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MC_WRREQ_LEVEL  :  The sum of the number of EA write requests in flight.  This is primarily meant for measure average EA write latency.  Average write latency = GL2C_PERF_SEL_MC_WRREQ_LEVEL/GL2C_PERF_SEL_MC_WRREQ. " = 0x5d, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_ATOMIC  :  Number of transactions going over the TC_EA_wrreq interface that are actually atomic requests. " = 0x5e, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_ATOMIC_LEVEL  :  The sum of the number of EA atomics in flight.  This is primarily meant for measure average EA atomic latency.  Average atomic latency = GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_ATOMIC_LEVEL/GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_ATOMIC. " = 0x5f, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MC_RDREQ  :  Number of GL2C/EA read requests (either 32-byte or 64-byte or 128-byte). " = 0x60, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_SNOOP  :  Number of GL2C/EA snoop read requests (either 32-byte or 64-byte or 128-byte). " = 0x61, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_SPLIT  :  Number of GL2C/EA read requests split due to non-contiguous sectors. " = 0x62, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_32B  :  Number of 32-byte GL2C/EA read requests " = 0x63, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_64B  :  Number of 64-byte GL2C/EA read requests " = 0x64, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_96B  :  Number of 96-byte GL2C/EA read requests " = 0x65, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_128B  :  Number of 128-byte GL2C/EA read requests " = 0x66, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RD_UNCACHED_32B  :  Number of 32-byte GL2C/EA read due to uncached traffic. A 64-byte request will be counted as 2; 96-byte as 3 and 128-byte as 4. " = 0x67, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RD_MDC_32B  :  Number of 32-byte GL2C/EA read due to MDC traffic.  A 64-byte request will be counted as 2 " = 0x68, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RD_COMPRESSED_32B  :  Number of 32-byte GL2C/EA read due to compressed data reads.  This does not include MDC traffic.  A 64-byte request will be counted as 2; 96-byte as 3 and 128-byte as 4. " = 0x69, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_IO_CREDIT_STALL  :  Number of cycles there was a stall because the read request interface was out of IO credits.  Stalls occur regardless of whether a read needed to be performed or not. " = 0x6a, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_GMI_CREDIT_STALL  :  Number of cycles there was a stall because the read request interface was out of GMI credits.  Stalls occur regardless of whether a read needed to be performed or not. " = 0x6b, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_DRAM_CREDIT_STALL  :  Number of cycles there was a stall because the read request interface was out of DRAM credits.  Stalls occur regardless of whether a read needed to be performed or not. " = 0x6c, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MC_RDREQ_LEVEL  :  The sum of the number of GL2C/EA read requests in flight.   This is primarily meant for measure average EA read latency.  Average read latency = GL2C_PERF_SEL_MC_RDREQ_LEVEL/GL2C_PERF_SEL_MC_RDREQ. " = 0x6d, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_DRAM  :  Number of GL2C/EA read requests (either 32-byte, 64-byte, 96-byte or 128-byte) destined for DRAM (MC). " = 0x6e, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_DRAM  :  Number of GL2C/EA write requests (either 32-byte, 64-byte, 96-byte or 128-byte) destined for DRAM (MC). " = 0x6f, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDREQ_DRAM_32B  :  Number of 32-byte GL2C/EA read due to dram traffic. A 64-byte request will be counted as 2; 96-byte as 3 and 128-byte as 4. " = 0x70, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRREQ_DRAM_32B  :  Number of 32-byte GL2C/EA write due to dram traffic. A 64-byte request will be counted as 2. " = 0x71, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ONION_READ  :  Number of read requests to GL2 onion VC (applies only in BC mode, bc=1 and spa=1 and snoop=1 and io=0). " = 0x72, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ONION_WRITE  :  Number of write requests to GL2 onion VC (applies only in BC mode, bc=1 and spa=1 and snoop=1 and io=0). " = 0x73, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_IO_READ  :  Number of read requests to GL2 IO VC. " = 0x74, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_IO_WRITE  :  Number of write requests to GL2 IO VC. " = 0x75, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GARLIC_READ  :  Number of read requests to GL2 garlic VC (~IO & ~ONION). " = 0x76, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GARLIC_WRITE  :  Number of write requests to GL2 garlic VC (~IO & ~ONION). " = 0x77, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_OUTSTANDING  :  Number of cycles when there is any outstanding EA request. " = 0x78, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_LATENCY_FIFO_FULL  :  Number of cycles the latency fifo was full. " = 0x79, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_SRC_FIFO_FULL  :  Number of cycles the src fifo was expected to be full as measured at the IB block. " = 0x7a, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled for any reason.  Normally, stalls of this nature are measured exactly from one point the pipeline, but that is not the case for this counter.  Probes can stall the pipeline at a variety of places, and there is no single point that can reasonably measure the total stalls accurately. " = 0x7b, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_WRITEBACK_FIFO_FULL_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled due to the writeback fifo within the tag block being full. " = 0x7c, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_MISS_NOTHING_REPLACEABLE_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled due to a cache miss and unavailabiliyt of a replaceable cache line. " = 0x7d, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_UNCACHED_WRITE_ATOMIC_FIFO_FULL_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled due to the uncached write/atomic fifo being full. " = 0x7e, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_NO_UNCACHED_WRITE_ATOMIC_ENTRIES_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled due to the lack of unused uncached write/atomic tracking entries. " = 0x7f, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_PROBE_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled due to the presence of a probe. " = 0x80, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_PROBE_FILTER_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled due to the probe filter being in an inappropriate state. " = 0x81, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_PROBE_FIFO_FULL_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled due to the probe fifo begin full. " = 0x82, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_TAG_READ_DST_STALL  :  Number of cycles the normal request pipeline in the tag was stalled due to the outstanding in-flight requests on an invalided cache line. " = 0x83, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_READ_RETURN_TIMEOUT  :  Number of bubbles requests sent to the GL2A because a EA read return waited so long for a cache ram port that it timed out. " = 0x84, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_WRITEBACK_READ_TIMEOUT  :  Number of bubbles requests sent to the GL2A because a writeback waited so long for a cache ram port that it timed out. " = 0x85, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_READ_RETURN_FULL_BUBBLE  :  Number of bubbles requests sent to the GL2A to prevent the EA read return fifos from overflowing.  Not windowable. " = 0x86, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_BUBBLE  :  Total number of bubble requests sent to the GL2A " = 0x87, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_IB_REQ  :  Number of requests through the IB.  This measures the raw request count from graphics clients going to this GL2C. " = 0x88, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_IB_STALL  :  Number of cycles the IB output was stalled. " = 0x89, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_IB_TAG_STALL  :  Number of cycles the IB output was stalled on the tag. " = 0x8a, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_IB_CM_STALL  :  Number of cycles the IB output was stalled on the mdc. " = 0x8b, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_RETURN_ACK  :  Number of times only an ack was sent on the return bus. " = 0x8c, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_RETURN_DATA  :  Number of times only data was sent on the return bus. " = 0x8d, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_RDRET_NACK  :  The number of EA read returns that were nacked. " = 0x8e, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_EA_WRRET_NACK  :  The number of EA write returns that were nacked. " = 0x8f, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GL2A_LEVEL  :  The sum of the number of requests sent to the GL2A for output arbitration in flight.  Average GL2A arbitration latency = GL2C_PERF_SEL_GL2A_LEVEL/GL2C_PERF_SEL_REQ. " = 0x90, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_PROBE_FILTER_DISABLE_TRANSITION  :  Number of times the probe filter went from enabled to disabled. " = 0x91, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_PROBE_FILTER_DISABLED  :  Number of cycles the probe filter was disabled.  The GL2C can get probes during these cycles.  Not windowable. " = 0x92, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ALL_TC_OP_WB_OR_INV_START  :  Number of gcr writeback or invalidate all requests started. " = 0x93, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ALL_TC_OP_WB_OR_INV_VOL_START  :  Number of gcr writeback or invalidate all volatile requests started. " = 0x94, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_INV  :  Number of gcr requests has invalidate field set. " = 0x95, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_WB  :  Number of gcr requests has writeback field set. " = 0x96, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_DISCARD  :  Number of gcr requests has discard field set. " = 0x97, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_RANGE  :  Number of gcr requests are range based. " = 0x98, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_ALL  :  Number of gcr requests are targeting on all cache lines. " = 0x99, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_VOL  :  Number of gcr requests are targeting on all volatile cache lines. " = 0x9a, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_UNSHARED  :  Number of gcr requests has unshared field set. " = 0x9b, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_MDC_INV  :  Number of gcr requests has metadata invalidation field set. " = 0x9c, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_GL2_INV_ALL  :  Number of gcr invalidate all gl2 requests. " = 0x9d, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_GL2_WB_ALL  :  Number of gcr writeback all gl2 requests. " = 0x9e, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_MDC_INV_ALL  :  Number of gcr metadata cache invalidate all requests. " = 0x9f, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_GL2_INV_RANGE  :  Number of gcr invalidate gl2 ranged requests. " = 0xa0, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_GL2_WB_RANGE  :  Number of gcr writeback gl2 ranged requests. " = 0xa1, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_GL2_WB_INV_RANGE  :  Number of gcr writeback and invalidate gl2 ranged requests. " = 0xa2, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_MDC_INV_RANGE  :  Number of gcr metadata cache invalidate ranged requests. " = 0xa3, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ALL_GCR_INV_EVICT  :  Number of cache line evictions/invalidations due to gcr request. " = 0xa4, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ALL_GCR_INV_VOL_EVICT  :  Number of volatile cache line evictions/invalidations due to gcr request.  " = 0xa5, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ALL_GCR_WB_OR_INV_CYCLE  :  Number of cycles spent performing gcr requests in tag pipeline. " = 0xa6, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ALL_GCR_WB_OR_INV_VOL_CYCLE  :  Number of cycles spent performing gcr volatile requests in tag pipeline. " = 0xa7, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_ALL_GCR_WB_WRITEBACK  :  Number of cache line writeback due to gcr request. " = 0xa8, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_INVL2_VOL_CYCLE  :  Number of cycles spent performing gcr INVL2_VOL requests in tag pipeline. " = 0xa9, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_INVL2_VOL_EVICT  :  Number of cache line evictions/invalidations due to INVL2_VOL requests. " = 0xaa, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_INVL2_VOL_START  :  Number of gcr INVL2_VOL requests. " = 0xab, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_WBL2_VOL_CYCLE  :  Number of cycles spent performing gcr WBL2_VOL requests in tag pipeline. " = 0xac, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_WBL2_VOL_START  :  Number of gcr WBL2_VOL requests. " = 0xad, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_WBINVL2_CYCLE  :  Number of cycles spent performing gcr WBINVL2 requests in tag pipeline. " = 0xae, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_WBINVL2_EVICT  :  Number of cache line evictions/invalidations due to WBINVL2 requests. " = 0xaf, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_GCR_WBINVL2_START  :  Number of gcr WBINVL2 requests. " = 0xb0, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_INV_METADATA  :  Number of cycles spent performing gcr requests in metadata tag. " = 0xb1, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_REQ  :  Number of requests passed through the metadata cache. " = 0xb2, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_LEVEL  :  The sum of the number of mdc requests in flight.  Average MDC latency=GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_LEVEL/GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_REQ. " = 0xb3, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_TAG_HIT  :  Number of MDC tag hits.  A tag contains multiple sectors, so many tag hits will be sector misses. " = 0xb4, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_SECTOR_HIT  :  Number of MDC sector hits.  A sector hit means that there actually is data in the cache for this request. " = 0xb5, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_SECTOR_MISS  :  Number of MDC sector misses. " = 0xb6, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_TAG_STALL  :  Number of cycles that the mdc tag is stalled. " = 0xb7, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_TAG_REPLACEMENT_LINE_IN_USE_STALL  :  Number of cycles that the mdc tag is stalled because the line to be replaced is stalled. " = 0xb8, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_TAG_DESECTORIZATION_FIFO_FULL_STALL  :  Number of cycles that the mdc tag is stalled because the desctorization fifo is full. " = 0xb9, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_MDC_TAG_WAITING_FOR_INVALIDATE_COMPLETION_STALL  :  Number of cycles that the mdc tag is stalled because it is waiting for the previous invalidate to complete. " = 0xba, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_CM_CHANNEL0_REQ  :  Number of compressed requests are distributed to channel0. " = 0xbb, 
                            "GL2C_PERF_SEL_CM_CHANNEL1_REQ" = 0xbc, 
