                            "PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT    Number of clocks where a PA_SC3 transactions does NOT occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC, starting AFTER the first prim following the PERFCOUNTER_START; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xb0, 
                            "PERF_PA_VERTEX_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_VERTEX_FIFO_FULL     Number of clocks when the vertex fifo in the legacy PA is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to help in NGG performance analysis by indicating backpressure from the vertex path of the legacy PA.  all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_PA_PRIMIC_TO_CLPRIM_FIFO_FULL count " = 0xb1, 
                            "PERF_PA_PRIMIC_TO_CLPRIM_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_PRIMIC_TO_CLPRIM_FIFO_FULL     Number of clocks when the primic_to_clprimx fifo in the legacy PA is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to help in NGG performance analysis by indicating backpressure from the position path of the legacy PA.  all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_PA_VERTEX_FIFO_FULL count " = 0xb2, 
                            "PERF_PA_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the NGG prim output fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used in perfornamce analysis and to help in finding the source of hangs.  all instances report the same result " = 0xb3, 
                            "PERF_PA_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the NGG position output fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used in perfornamce analysis and to help in finding the source of hangs. all instances report the same result " = 0xb4, 
                            "PERF_PA_PIPE0_SWITCHED_GEN  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_PIPE0_SWITCHED_GEN    Number of times the PA has processed a pipe0 primitive that belongs to a different GEN than did the previously processed primitive;  range-1/generation_switch; all instances report the same result " = 0xb5, 
                            "PERF_PA_PIPE1_SWITCHED_GEN  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_PIPE1_SWITCHED_GEN    Number of times the PA has processed a pipe1 primitive that belongs to a different GEN than did the previously processed primitive;  range-1/generation_switch; all instances report the same result " = 0xb6, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_IS_STARVED  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_IS_STARVED    Number of clocks when the PA CSB machine is starved for work; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xb7, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_STALLED_BY_CSB_MEMORY  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_STALLED_BY_CSB_MEMORY    Number of clocks when the PA CSB machine has a control sideband ready to be written to CSB memory, but the memory is full; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xb8, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_STALLED_BY_SPI  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_STALLED_BY_SPI    Number of clocks when the PA CSB machine has a control sideband and payload from the GE but is waiting on the SPI to provide vert/prim counts; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xb9, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_INPUT_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_INPUT_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the PA CSB GE input fifo is full, and the PA will now be appying backpressure to the GE; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xba, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_SPI_INPUT_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_SPI_INPUT_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the PA CSB SPI input fifo is full;  range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbb, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_PAYLOAD_INPUT_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_PAYLOAD_INPUT_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the PA payload input fifo is full; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbc, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_INPUT_FIFO_POP_BIT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_INPUT_FIFO_POP_BIT    Number of times when the PA receives a subgroup that contains a pop bit to the payload fifo.  Events are not counted; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbd, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_PRIM_COUNT_EQ0  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_PRIM_COUNT_EQ0    Number of times when the PA recieves a CSB with a prim count of zero; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbe, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_NULL_SUBGROUP  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_NULL_SUBGROUP    Number of times when the PA recieves a CSB that has been marked as a null subgroup.  Events are not counted.; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbf, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_SENDING_SUBGROUP  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_SENDING_SUBGROUP    Number of times when the PA recieves a CSB from the GE that represents a subgroup; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc0, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_MEMORY_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_MEMORY_FULL    Number of clocks when the GE CSB memory is full.; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc1, 
