                            "PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT    Number of PA_SC0 transactions that have occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xa9, 
                            "PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT    Number of clocks where a PA_SC0 transactions does NOT occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC, starting AFTER the first prim following the PERFCOUNTER_START; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xaa, 
