                            "PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_NX1  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_NX1     Number of pixels that have been culled by small prim filter whose bounding box fits within 4 or more horizontal by 1 vertical pixels; range-1/clk; it can be used as a subset of PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT to measure the number of culled prims as a function of primitive size; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT and the other PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_nXn counts " = 0xa2, 
                            "PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_1XN  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_1XN     Number of pixels that have been culled by small prim filter whose bounding box fits within 1 horizontal by 4 or more vertical pixels; range-1/clk; it can be used as a subset of PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT to measure the number of culled prims as a function of primitive size; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT and the other PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_nXn counts " = 0xa3, 
                            "PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_NX2  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_NX2     Number of pixels that have been culled by small prim filter whose bounding box fits within 4 or more horizontal by 2 vertical pixels; range-1/clk; it can be used as a subset of PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT to measure the number of culled prims as a function of primitive size; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT and the other PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_nXn counts " = 0xa4, 
                            "PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_2XN  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_2XN     Number of pixels that have been culled by small prim filter whose bounding box fits within 2 horizontal by 4 or more vertical pixels; range-1/clk; it can be used as a subset of PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT to measure the number of culled prims as a function of primitive size; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT and the other PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_nXn counts " = 0xa5, 
                            "PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_FULL_RES_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_FULL_RES_EVENT    Number of pixels that have been culled by small prim filter whose bounding box lies fully within the full resolution region, and/or the foveated region; range-1/clk; it can be used as a subset of PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT to measure the number of culled prims as a function of primitive location; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT and the PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_nXn counts " = 0xa6, 
                            "PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_HALF_RES_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_HALF_RES_EVENT    Number of pixels that have been culled by small prim filter whose bounding box lies fully within one of the eight regions that surround the center region; range-1/clk; it can be used as a subset of PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT to measure the number of culled prims as a function of primitive location; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT and the PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_nXn counts " = 0xa7, 
                            "PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_QUARTER_RES_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_QUARTER_RES_EVENT    Number of pixels that have been culled by small prim filter whose bounding box lies fully within one of the remaining 16 outer regions; range-1/clk; it can be used as a subset of PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT to measure the number of culled prims as a function of primitive location; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT and the PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_nXn counts " = 0xa8, 
                            "PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT    Number of PA_SC0 transactions that have occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xa9, 
                            "PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT    Number of clocks where a PA_SC0 transactions does NOT occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC, starting AFTER the first prim following the PERFCOUNTER_START; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC0_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xaa, 
                            "PERF_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT    Number of PA_SC1 transactions that have occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xab, 
                            "PERF_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT    Number of clocks where a PA_SC1 transactions does NOT occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC, starting AFTER the first prim following the PERFCOUNTER_START; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC1_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xac, 
                            "PERF_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT    Number of PA_SC2 transactions that have occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xad, 
                            "PERF_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT    Number of clocks where a PA_SC2 transactions does NOT occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC, starting AFTER the first prim following the PERFCOUNTER_START; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC2_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xae, 
                            "PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT    Number of PA_SC3 transactions that have occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xaf, 
                            "PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT    Number of clocks where a PA_SC3 transactions does NOT occurred between the time a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event have been sent to the SC, starting AFTER the first prim following the PERFCOUNTER_START; range-1/clk; this can be used with PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT to measure primitive transfer rate between PA and SC; all instances report the same result; the sum of PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_BUSY_EVENT and PERF_SC3_QUALIFIED_SEND_NOT_BUSY_EVENT is equal to the total number of clocks between START/STOP events, after the first transaction following PERFCOUNTER_START has occurred " = 0xb0, 
                            "PERF_PA_VERTEX_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_VERTEX_FIFO_FULL     Number of clocks when the vertex fifo in the legacy PA is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to help in NGG performance analysis by indicating backpressure from the vertex path of the legacy PA.  all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_PA_PRIMIC_TO_CLPRIM_FIFO_FULL count " = 0xb1, 
                            "PERF_PA_PRIMIC_TO_CLPRIM_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_PRIMIC_TO_CLPRIM_FIFO_FULL     Number of clocks when the primic_to_clprimx fifo in the legacy PA is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to help in NGG performance analysis by indicating backpressure from the position path of the legacy PA.  all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_PA_VERTEX_FIFO_FULL count " = 0xb2, 
                            "PERF_PA_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the NGG prim output fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used in perfornamce analysis and to help in finding the source of hangs.  all instances report the same result " = 0xb3, 
                            "PERF_PA_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the NGG position output fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used in perfornamce analysis and to help in finding the source of hangs. all instances report the same result " = 0xb4, 
                            "PERF_PA_PIPE0_SWITCHED_GEN  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_PIPE0_SWITCHED_GEN    Number of times the PA has processed a pipe0 primitive that belongs to a different GEN than did the previously processed primitive;  range-1/generation_switch; all instances report the same result " = 0xb5, 
                            "PERF_PA_PIPE1_SWITCHED_GEN  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_PA_PIPE1_SWITCHED_GEN    Number of times the PA has processed a pipe1 primitive that belongs to a different GEN than did the previously processed primitive;  range-1/generation_switch; all instances report the same result " = 0xb6, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_IS_STARVED  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_IS_STARVED    Number of clocks when the PA CSB machine is starved for work; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xb7, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_STALLED_BY_CSB_MEMORY  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_STALLED_BY_CSB_MEMORY    Number of clocks when the PA CSB machine has a control sideband ready to be written to CSB memory, but the memory is full; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xb8, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_STALLED_BY_SPI  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_MACHINE_STALLED_BY_SPI    Number of clocks when the PA CSB machine has a control sideband and payload from the GE but is waiting on the SPI to provide vert/prim counts; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xb9, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_INPUT_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_INPUT_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the PA CSB GE input fifo is full, and the PA will now be appying backpressure to the GE; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xba, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_SPI_INPUT_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_SPI_INPUT_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the PA CSB SPI input fifo is full;  range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbb, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_PAYLOAD_INPUT_FIFO_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_PAYLOAD_INPUT_FIFO_FULL    Number of clocks when the PA payload input fifo is full; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbc, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_INPUT_FIFO_POP_BIT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_INPUT_FIFO_POP_BIT    Number of times when the PA receives a subgroup that contains a pop bit to the payload fifo.  Events are not counted; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbd, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_PRIM_COUNT_EQ0  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_PRIM_COUNT_EQ0    Number of times when the PA recieves a CSB with a prim count of zero; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbe, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_NULL_SUBGROUP  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_NULL_SUBGROUP    Number of times when the PA recieves a CSB that has been marked as a null subgroup.  Events are not counted.; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xbf, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_SENDING_SUBGROUP  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_SENDING_SUBGROUP    Number of times when the PA recieves a CSB from the GE that represents a subgroup; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc0, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_MEMORY_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_MEMORY_FULL    Number of clocks when the GE CSB memory is full.; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc1, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_GE_MEMORY_EMPTY  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_GE_MEMORY_EMPTY    Number of clocks when the GE CSB memory is empty.; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc2, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_SPI_MEMORY_FULL  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_SPI_MEMORY_FULL    Number of clocks when the SPI CSB memory is full.; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc3, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_SPI_MEMORY_EMPTY  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_SPI_MEMORY_EMPTY    Number of clocks when the SPI CSB memory is empty.; range-1/csb; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc4, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN00  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN00    Number of clocks on average between GE_PA_csb_send signals.  Resolution R set by PA_CL_ENHANCE.TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION.  Each count represents an average of R/2 clocks; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc5, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN01  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN01    Number of clocks on average between GE_PA_csb_send signals.  Resolution R set by PA_CL_ENHANCE.TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION.  Each count represents an average of R clocks; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc6, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN02  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN02    Number of clocks on average between GE_PA_csb_send signals.  Resolution R set by PA_CL_ENHANCE.TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION.  Each count represents an average of 2*R clocks; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc7, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN03  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN03    Number of clocks on average between GE_PA_csb_send signals.  Resolution R set by PA_CL_ENHANCE.TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION.  Each count represents an average of 3*R clocks; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc8, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN04  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN04    Number of clocks on average between GE_PA_csb_send signals.  Resolution R set by PA_CL_ENHANCE.TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION.  Each count represents an average of 4*R clocks; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xc9, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN05  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN05    Number of clocks on average between GE_PA_csb_send signals.  Resolution R set by PA_CL_ENHANCE.TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION.  Each count represents an average of 5*R clocks; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xca, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN06  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_CSB_DELAY_BIN06    Number of clocks on average between GE_PA_csb_send signals.  Resolution R set by PA_CL_ENHANCE.TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION.  Each count represents an average of 6*R clocks; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0xcb, 
