                            "PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_FULL_RES_EVENT  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_FULL_RES_EVENT    Number of pixels that have been culled by small prim filter whose bounding box lies fully within the full resolution region, and/or the foveated region; range-1/clk; it can be used as a subset of PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT to measure the number of culled prims as a function of primitive location; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the PERF_SU_SMALL_PRIM_FILTER_CULL_CNT and the PERF_SMALL_PRIM_CULL_PRIM_nXn counts " = 0xa6, 
