                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_RET_SXRX_READING_QDWORD_3_NULL_PRIMS  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_INDEX_RET_SXRX_READING_QDWORD_3_NULL_PRIMS    Number of times the index sx return logic has received a qdword from the SX with 3 valid prims. ; range-1/qdword; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x100, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_RET_SXRX_READING_QDWORD_4_NULL_PRIMS  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_INDEX_RET_SXRX_READING_QDWORD_4_NULL_PRIMS    Number of times the index sx return logic has received a qdword from the SX with 4 valid prims. ; range-1/qdword; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x101, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_STALLED_BY_FULL_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_STALLED_BY_FULL_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO    Number of clocks when the index prim interface logic is being stalled by a full fetch_to_primic_p fifo; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x102, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_STALLED_BY_FULL_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_S_FIFO  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_STALLED_BY_FULL_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_S_FIFO    Number of clocks when the index prim interface logic is being stalled by a full fetch_to_primic_s fifo; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x103, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_STARVED_BY_NO_CSB  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_STARVED_BY_NO_CSB    Number of clocks when the index prim interface logic is being starved and is waiting for a control sideband from the index sx receive logic; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x104, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_STARVED_BY_NO_PRIM  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_STARVED_BY_NO_PRIM    Number of clocks when the index prim interface logic is being starved and is waiting for a prim from the index sx receive logic; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x105, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_WRITE  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_WRITE    Number of clocks the index prim interface logic is writing a prim the the legacy PA prim interface, and qualified by busy; range-1/clock; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x106, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_NO_WRITE  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_INDEX_PRIM_IF_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_NO_WRITE    Number of clocks the index prim interface logic is not writing a prim the the legacy PA prim interface, and qualified by busy; range-1/clock; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x107, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_POS_REQ_STARVED  :  PAPC_PERF_SEL_ENGG_POS_REQ_STARVED    Number of clocks the NGG position request machine is starved waiting for a valid CSB; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x108, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_INDEX_RET_SXRX_NULL_DROPPER_STALLED_BY_FULL_PRIM_FIFO  :  PERF_ENGG_INDEX_RET_SXRX_NULL_DROPPER_STALLED_BY_FULL_PRIM_FIFO   Number of clocks the NGG index SX return null dropping logic is being stalled by its output fifo being full. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x109, 
                            "PERF_ENGG_BUSY  :  PERF_ENGG_BUSY   Number of clocks the NGG logic is reporting busy. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf and power analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x10a, 
                            "PERF_CLIPSM_CULL_PRIMS_CNT  :  PERF_CLIPSM_CULL_PRIMS_CNT   Number of prims culled by the clipper; range 1-/clk; can be used in clipper perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x10b, 
                            "PERF_PH_SEND_1_SC  :  PERF_PH_SEND_1_SC   Number of clocks where PA_PH_data_send is asserted directing traffic to 1 SC. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x10c, 
                            "PERF_PH_SEND_2_SC  :  PERF_PH_SEND_2_SC   Number of clocks where PA_PH_data_send is asserted directing traffic to 2 SCs. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x10d, 
                            "PERF_PH_SEND_3_SC  :  PERF_PH_SEND_3_SC   Number of clocks where PA_PH_data_send is asserted directing traffic to 3 SCs. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x10e, 
                            "PERF_PH_SEND_4_SC  :  PERF_PH_SEND_4_SC   Number of clocks where PA_PH_data_send is asserted directing traffic to 4 SCs. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x10f, 
                            "PERF_OUTPUT_PRIM_1_SC  :  PERF_OUTPUT_PRIM_1_SC   Number of clocks where a valid prim is being sent to 1 SC. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x110, 
                            "PERF_OUTPUT_PRIM_2_SC  :  PERF_OUTPUT_PRIM_2_SC   Number of clocks where a valid prim is being sent to 2 SCs. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x111, 
                            "PERF_OUTPUT_PRIM_3_SC  :  PERF_OUTPUT_PRIM_3_SC   Number of clocks where a valid prim is being sent to 3 SCs. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x112, 
                            "PERF_OUTPUT_PRIM_4_SC  :  PERF_OUTPUT_PRIM_4_SC   Number of clocks where a valid prim is being sent to 4 SCs. ; range-1/clk; can be used in NGG perf analysis.  All instances report the same result " = 0x113 }  ;
    PERF_MODE3  27:24  ALPHA {"PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_ACCUM  :  Accumulate increment values over enabled cycles. " = 0x0, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_ACTIVE_CYCLES  :  Count the number of cycles with a nonzero increment value. " = 0x1, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_MAX  :  Store the largest increment value received over cycles counted. " = 0x2, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_DIRTY  :  Record whether a nonzero increment value was ever received. " = 0x3, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_SAMPLE  :  Just record the latest increment vlaue. " = 0x4, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_SINCE_FIRST_EVENT  :  Count the cycles since a nonzero increment value. " = 0x5, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_SINCE_LAST_EVENT  :  Count the cycles since a zero increment value. " = 0x6, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_GE_HI  :  Count the cycles with an increment greater than or equal to the value in the high bits. " = 0x7, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_EQ_HI  :  Count the cycles with an increment equal to the value in the high bits. " = 0x8, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_INACTIVE_CYCLES  :  Count the number of cycles with a zero increment value. " = 0x9, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_RESERVED  :  This is here just so this is a 4 bit field in case we add modes in the future.  Don't use it. " = 0xf }  ;
    PERF_MODE2  31:28  ALPHA {"PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_ACCUM  :  Accumulate increment values over enabled cycles. " = 0x0, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_ACTIVE_CYCLES  :  Count the number of cycles with a nonzero increment value. " = 0x1, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_MAX  :  Store the largest increment value received over cycles counted. " = 0x2, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_DIRTY  :  Record whether a nonzero increment value was ever received. " = 0x3, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_SAMPLE  :  Just record the latest increment vlaue. " = 0x4, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_SINCE_FIRST_EVENT  :  Count the cycles since a nonzero increment value. " = 0x5, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_SINCE_LAST_EVENT  :  Count the cycles since a zero increment value. " = 0x6, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_GE_HI  :  Count the cycles with an increment greater than or equal to the value in the high bits. " = 0x7, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_EQ_HI  :  Count the cycles with an increment equal to the value in the high bits. " = 0x8, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_INACTIVE_CYCLES  :  Count the number of cycles with a zero increment value. " = 0x9, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_RESERVED  :  This is here just so this is a 4 bit field in case we add modes in the future.  Don't use it. " = 0xf }  ;
